    "document": "Core Rules",
    "section": "09. Movement Phase",
    "ruleNumber": "09.02",
    "summary": "The active player moves units 1 at a time until each has been picked to move and has finished. For each unit:\n\n1. Pick a friendly unit not yet picked to move in this phase; it can be in **strategic reserves**, on the battlefield or embarked in a **TRANSPORT**.\n2. Choose a move type it is eligible for and resolve it: **[Remain stationary](vsdata:core-rule/remain-stationary)**, **[Normal move](vsdata:core-rule/normal-move)**, **[Advance move](vsdata:core-rule/advance-move)**, **[Fall-back move](vsdata:core-rule/fall-back)**, **[Disembark move](vsdata:core-rule/disembark-move)**, **[Ingress move](vsdata:core-rule/ingress-move)** or one from another rule.\n\nBy the end of the step every unit, strategic reserves included, must have been picked; a unit given no move type remains stationary.\n\nWhere a rule has you pick a mode, as fall-back moves do:\n\n- Modes exclude each other; check them in the order given.\n- A unit that meets no mode’s conditions cannot make that move.\n- Some modes are mandatory when they apply (such as consolidation modes); **ordered retreat** is not, so **desperate escape** may be picked instead.\n- A condition tagged with a mode’s name applies only when that mode was picked; untagged conditions always apply.\n\nAnything a rule places in the Reinforcements step happens during this step.",
